  "body": "## Contribution\n\nThis PR records an exact P104 construction change based on PR #2152 at `05f7aad0f08992ee48ec2dd93e896d9a4567847d`. The predecessor is still open, so this PR carries a source-pinned patch and replay package instead of duplicating its full source tree.\n\nOn the original `fanout.py` word, the existing private copy for pair `(4,57)` descends through the three nested contact frames for public helper 7, supplies those live-Y contacts, then continues to `La` to seed the remaining helpers. The helper register stays allocated and untouched. The full 735-input endpoint map passes exact rational replay and native lowering.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Combined transport rank mass decreases from 5,894 to 5,885; private COPY mass remains 56.\n- Scalar ADD count decreases from 20,956 to 20,947. Seven entry-compensation ADDs and one each of helper seed and helper restoration disappear; three direct private contacts replace three public contact ADDs.\n- The exact selected-threshold moment remains greater than one. The optimistic complex-side cap is `0.00165874758371416805798661`, below selected `\u03ba = 0.001672660197076918`. This is a local cost reduction, not an improved \u03ba or supplier.\n- Native replay passes 3,743 transport occurrences, 3,050 distinct recipes, all eight private paths, and 4,096 Gaussian basis columns; the wrong-phase control rejects.\n- Five scalar negative controls reject, including omission of one reused contact.\n\n## Scope and reproduction\n\nThe initial Discussion claim called the target word \u201ccoalesced.\u201d The checked experiment applies to PR #2152's original `fanout.py` word before its separate `coalesced.py` rechart; the coalesced variant remains untested. This package records that scope correction and pins the exact patch, source hashes, cost inputs, and replay receipts.\n\nSee `research/p104-private-descent-reuse-seed915fa969/README.md` for reproduction commands, exact moment and root intervals, predecessor attribution, and remaining obligations. No selected frontier change, merge, or \u03ba claim is requested.\n",
